/// Every codepoint from every face, **plus** the procedural Box Drawing range.
///
/// The Box Drawing chain is here even though no face carries those codepoints, and that is
/// the point: the atlas is built for the union of what is rasterised from fonts and what is
/// drawn procedurally, so the ranges a caller must be able to *address* include both. Phase
/// 9B's first regeneration dropped this chain, and `every_required_codepoint_resolves_in_every_face`
/// immediately reported 497 codepoints where it expected 625 -- the 128 Box Drawing slots
/// simply had no index. A generated file that quietly loses a function is why this script
/// exists rather than the Rust being hand-edited in the other direction.
pub fn codepoints_all() -> impl Iterator<Item = u32> {
    codepoints_in_text_ranges()
        .chain(codepoints_in_math_ranges())
        .chain(BOX_RANGE.0..=BOX_RANGE.1)
}

// NOTE: an earlier version of Phase 8 added a `build_atlas` *here*, duplicating
// [`crate::build_atlas`]. That was wrong twice over. It returned `Atlas` where the real one returns
// `(Atlas, BootReport)`, so every caller silently dropped the phase timings -- including the one that
// measures boot. And it decompressed into a plain `Vec<u8>` where the real one decompresses into a
// page-locked, `mlock`ed, zeroizing `SecureBlock`, which is the entire point of Phase 4's
// one-time pass: the expanded fonts are *supposed* to be scrubbed, and the duplicate made them
// ordinary heap that a later `Drop` would leave behind.
//
// There is one `build_atlas`. It lives at the crate root because it is the whole pass, not a
// payload detail, and it is the only place that knows the phases have to happen in order.
